From 9e3e2e02cd69f9ace0b13e462df462a8496e8845 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SkillBuddy Agent <agent@skillbuddy.local>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 21:39:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Live-testing fixes round 2: dark-mode crash cascade, welcome
 banner removed, logo size, guaranteed navigation loader, Manrope font,
 language system foundation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Dark mode: found and fixed two more screens hardcoded to colors.light
  regardless of theme (booking/[id].tsx, profile/edit.tsx, chat/[id].tsx)
  — day/time selectors, message bubbles, input bars, and form fields
  all now correctly follow the active theme. Also fixed SkeletonCard,
  which was always rendering light-theme skeleton colors.

- Removed the 'Welcome back, Name' banner entirely from Home per
  request — the section now leads directly with 'What service do you
  need today?' promoted to a proper heading.

- Increased the logo size on Home and Profile headers (42px/40px ->
  54px/52px) for a more prominent, properly-filled brand presence.

- Added NavigationLoaderOverlay: a global route-change listener that
  now guarantees a brief branded loading state on every single
  navigation, app-wide, instead of relying on manually wiring a loader
  into each screen one at a time. Explicitly skips the transparent
  filter modal so it doesn't defeat that screen's see-through backdrop.

- Swapped the app's font from Inter to Manrope across all ~330
  occurrences in 45 files (a friendlier, more distinctive geometric
  sans that suits a services-marketplace brand better than a generic
  UI font). Requires Scope: all 9 workspace projects
✓ Lockfile passes supply-chain policies (verified 4m ago)
Lockfile is up to date, resolution step is skipped
Already up to date

. preinstall$ sh -c 'rm -f package-lock.json yarn.lock; case "$npm_config_user_agent" in pnpm/*) ;; *) echo "Use pnpm instead" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac'
. preinstall: Done
[ERR_PNPM_IGNORED_BUILDS] Ignored build scripts: esbuild@0.27.3

Run "pnpm approve-builds" to pick which dependencies should be allowed to run scripts. after applying this patch since
  it's a new font package.

- Added a LanguageContext foundation (5 languages: EN/DE/ET/LV/LT,
  persisted selection) and wired it into the tab bar labels and Home
  screen's key strings as a working proof of the system. Translating
  every remaining string across the app (~40 more screens) is a large
  follow-up task, tracked separately — not something that fits in this
  pass alongside everything else.

Full workspace typecheck: zero errors.
